-- Birbal docs for the order-to-cash bridge
delete from warehouse.warehouse_meta where table_name in ('o2c_bridge', 'o2c_invoices', 'o2c_bridge_live', 'o2c_invoices_live', 'o2c_credit_memos', 'o2c_grn_lines', 'ref_customer_invoicing');
insert into warehouse.warehouse_meta (table_name, doc_md) values
('o2c_bridge', $doc$CONTAINS CANCELLED INVOICES -- DO NOT USE BY DEFAULT. This view carries every FY27 invoice INCLUDING the cancelled ones (invoice_status = 'CANCELLED', ~200 invoices, Rs 1.2 cr of invoiced_value that was never really billed: the ERP cancels an invoice and re-issues it under the same PO with a suffix). A cancelled invoice must never be counted, listed, averaged or netted anywhere -- fill rate, shortage, sales, invoice lists, all of it. Query o2c_bridge_live instead, which is this view filtered to invoice_status = 'LIVE'. Use THIS view only when the question is itself about cancellations or re-invoicing.

ORDER-TO-CASH BRIDGE (line grain) -- PO -> Invoice -> GRN -> Credit Memo, one row per posted sales invoice x ERP item, FY27 (invoice posting date >= 2026-04-01; earlier invoices have no lines in Supabase). Refreshed by select public.o2c_refresh(); loaded_at is not stored, check max(invoice_date). Use this for "was the invoice received in full", "what is short and not yet credited", "which invoices did PO X produce". For invoice-level answers prefer o2c_invoices (same logic rolled up).

PO -> INVOICE. po_number is the customer PO with trailing junk removed (the ERP re-invoices a cancelled invoice under the same PO plus a suffix such as . ` ' _ ; po_number_raw keeps the original, po_suffixed = true marks these). po_invoice_pattern comes from ref_customer_invoicing: ONE_PO_ONE_INVOICE for every marketplace except First Club and for most trade accounts; ONE_PO_MANY_INVOICES for Reliance / Milkbasket, Nature's Basket, Namdhari's, Metro Cash & Carry, First Club and a few small trade accounts, where one PO is served by several invoices over days or weeks -- there, count invoices per PO, never assume one. invoice_status = LIVE or CANCELLED; a cancelled invoice carries cancellation_cm_no (the corrective credit memo) and replacement_invoice_no (the later live invoice on the same PO, 191 of 198 cases); the replacement carries replaces_invoice_no. Never add a cancelled invoice to sales. po_qty is the PO quantity as entered on the invoice line, invoiced_qty is what we billed (the ERP line Quantity), invoiced_value is ex-GST line amount. erp_item_no is the CURRENT item code: the ERP still posts about 7% of invoice and credit-memo lines under the old FG code of a renamed item, so invoice lines, GRN rows and credit-memo lines are all mapped through item_rename_map before they are compared (o2c_invoice_lines keeps the posted code in erp_item_no_raw).

INVOICE -> GRN. The partner GRN feeds are matched to the invoice by grn_match_method: invoice_exact (the feed carries our invoice number), invoice_core+po (the feed mangles the number -- '27 MUM-008049', '07685' -- so the 5-digit core plus the PO number is used), invoice_core, po_unique (1 PO : 1 invoice customers whose feed has no invoice number, e.g. Blinkit BCPL hot_grn), po+item+qty / po+item+date (1 PO : many invoices customers when the feed quotes the partner's own document number, e.g. Milkbasket 'MHB/26-27/15357'), po_ambiguous (could not be decided; treat as unknown). An invoice-number match (invoice_exact) needs the invoice's customer to be one of the feed's customers or the feed's PO to agree, and a 5-digit-core match (invoice_core+po, invoice_core) is refused when the GRN is dated more than 3 days before the invoice: invoice numbers restart every financial year, so 26BLR-09889 (Oct 2025) and 27BLR-09889 (Oct 2026) share a core. grn_coverage says what the GRN can tell you: ITEM_QTY (grn_qty is the partner's received/accepted units for this item, one copy per GRN row -- grn_duplicate_rows counts copies the feed loaded twice), ITEM_NOT_IN_GRN (the invoice's GRN was found and every item in it is identified, but this item is not in it: the partner did not receive it, so short_qty = invoiced_qty -- the SHGRN credit memos that exist for such lines credit the full quantity), INVOICE_ONLY (a GRN exists for the invoice but this item cannot be judged: Reliance's feed has no item lines, or some feed item codes are unmapped), NOT_FOUND (the customer has a feed but nothing matched this invoice, or every matched GRN row is still pending with nothing booked), NO_FEED (no GRN feed in Supabase: DMart, Metro Cash & Carry (received but not loaded), First Club, and trade accounts other than Nature's Basket and the Reliance stores -- the business receives no GRN from those), CANCELLED_INVOICE. Amazon (amazon_grn) and Zepto (zepto_grn) come from portal reports pasted into Google Sheets and are matched by PO + item; a Zepto line counts Zepto's GRN quantity once the line is closed or, while it is still PENDING_GRN / ASN_CREATED, once Zepto has booked a GRN quantity on it (grn_reject_reason 'grn booked, portal status ...'); a Zepto line still pending with nothing booked, or an Amazon PO still Unconfirmed, carries the pending state in grn_reject_reason; when every GRN row of the invoice is pending like that the invoice reads NOT_FOUND (GRN pending, not short), otherwise the line reads ITEM_NOT_IN_GRN. short_qty = invoiced_qty - grn_qty when positive, short_value at the invoice unit price, excess_qty when the partner booked more than invoiced (a second GRN on the same invoice line, or a re-receipt; treat as received in full). grn_rejected_qty / grn_reject_reason come from BigBasket, Nature's Basket and Blinkit ZHPL (damaged).

GRN -> CREDIT MEMO. shgrn_cm_nos / shgrn_cm_qty / shgrn_cm_value are the SHORT-GRN credit memos (reason code SHGRN) linked to this invoice and item. credit_status: GRN_FULL (received in full), SHORT_CREDITED (short and a SHGRN credit memo covers it), SHORT_PARTIALLY_CREDITED, SHORT_CREDIT_PENDING (short units with no credit memo yet -- the list finance should chase; recent invoices may simply be waiting), NOT_IN_GRN_CREDIT_PENDING (the whole item is missing from the partner's GRN and no credit memo exists -- the same chase list, kept separate because the shortage is inferred from absence rather than measured), SHORT_CREDITED_AT_INVOICE_LEVEL (a SHGRN memo exists on the invoice but not for this item), CREDITED_WITHOUT_SHORTAGE (memo issued although the GRN shows full receipt -- review), CREDITED_NO_GRN_VISIBILITY (a SHGRN memo exists but the feed cannot show the receipt), GRN_NOT_AVAILABLE (nothing to judge from), INVOICE_CANCELLED. Expiry returns, damage, INC, capping and reconciliation credit memos are NOT in this table; see o2c_credit_memos.

Columns: po_number, po_number_raw, po_suffixed, platform, customer_no, customer_name, customer_search_name, po_invoice_pattern, ship_to_code, ship_to_name, warehouse_code, so_no, invoice_no, invoice_date, invoice_status, cancellation_cm_no, replacement_invoice_no, replaces_invoice_no, erp_item_no, item_name, item_category, po_qty, invoiced_qty, unit_price, invoiced_value, grn_feed, grn_nos, grn_date, grn_qty, grn_rejected_qty, grn_reject_reason, grn_duplicate_rows, grn_match_method, grn_coverage, short_qty, excess_qty, short_value, shgrn_cm_nos, shgrn_cm_qty, shgrn_cm_value, credit_status
platform is resolved at ship-to level (channel_map_locations): Reliance Retail's RRL MILK BASKET locations appear as Milkbasket, its stores and DCs as Reliance. Group by platform and both come out as separate rows.$doc$),
('o2c_invoices', $doc$CONTAINS CANCELLED INVOICES -- DO NOT USE BY DEFAULT. This view carries every FY27 invoice INCLUDING the cancelled ones (invoice_status = 'CANCELLED', ~200 invoices, Rs 1.2 cr of invoiced_value that was never really billed: the ERP cancels an invoice and re-issues it under the same PO with a suffix). A cancelled invoice must never be counted, listed, averaged or netted anywhere -- fill rate, shortage, sales, invoice lists, all of it. Query o2c_invoices_live instead, which is this view filtered to invoice_status = 'LIVE'. Use THIS view only when the question is itself about cancellations or re-invoicing.

ORDER-TO-CASH BRIDGE (invoice grain) -- one row per posted sales invoice, FY27, rolled up from o2c_bridge: PO, customer, invoice status and replacement chain, item_lines, po_qty, invoiced_qty, invoiced_value, GRN feed / numbers / date / received qty, short_qty, excess_qty, short_value, SHORT-GRN credit memos and a single credit_status (worst line wins: INVOICE_CANCELLED > SHORT_CREDIT_PENDING > NOT_IN_GRN_CREDIT_PENDING > SHORT_PARTIALLY_CREDITED > SHORT_CREDITED > CREDITED_NO_GRN_VISIBILITY > GRN_FULL; PARTLY_VISIBLE_GRN_FULL = every visible line was received in full but some lines are not visible in the feed; GRN_NOT_AVAILABLE = no receipt data at all). lines_not_in_grn counts items absent from the partner's GRN. grn_coverage here is the weakest line's coverage. Same meanings as o2c_bridge, see that doc. Count invoices with count(*), POs with count(distinct (customer_no, po_number)).

Columns: po_number, po_number_raw, po_suffixed, platform, customer_no, customer_name, customer_search_name, po_invoice_pattern, ship_to_code, ship_to_name, warehouse_code, so_no, invoice_no, invoice_date, invoice_status, cancellation_cm_no, replacement_invoice_no, replaces_invoice_no, item_lines, po_qty, invoiced_qty, invoiced_value, grn_feed, grn_nos, grn_date, grn_qty, short_qty, excess_qty, short_value, lines_not_in_grn, grn_coverage, shgrn_cm_nos, shgrn_cm_qty, shgrn_cm_value, credit_status
platform is resolved at ship-to level (channel_map_locations): Reliance Retail's RRL MILK BASKET locations appear as Milkbasket, its stores and DCs as Reliance. Group by platform and both come out as separate rows.$doc$),
('o2c_credit_memos', $doc$LIVE ERP -- every posted sales credit memo from FY27 (document date >= 2026-04-01) categorised and linked to the invoice it credits. credit_memo_date is the memo's DOCUMENT date -- the same date the sales register attributes a memo by (effective_date, and so v_net_sales, the MIS, COGS and the P&L) -- so group and window by it; ledger_posting_date is the G/L posting date, for ledger reconciliation only. category: INVOICE_CANCELLATION (the corrective memo behind a cancelled invoice; the invoice is re-issued under the same PO with a suffix), SHORT_GRN (partner received less than invoiced; the memo that closes o2c_bridge short lines), EXPIRY_RETURN (stock returned at expiry -- the largest category by value, not tied to a specific invoice), DAMAGE, INC, FR, RECONCILIATION (RECO-CN), CAPPING_RETURN (Instamart return-to-vendor 'BAKERS-..RTV' documents), UNSPECIFIED. invoice_no / link_method: applies_to (the ERP Applies-to Doc No.), document_ref (External Document No. or PRN Document No. is our invoice number), po_unique (External Document No. is a PO with exactly one live invoice); null = not attributable to one invoice (normal for expiry and capping returns). po_number is the linked invoice's PO, else the memo's external document number cleaned. credit_memo_amount is the amount to customer. Never add credit memos to invoices; subtract.

Columns: credit_memo_no, customer_no, customer_name, credit_memo_date, credit_memo_amount, reason_code, is_cancellation, applies_to_doc_no, applies_to_doc_type, external_document_no, prn_document_no, prn_document_date, warehouse_code, ledger_posting_date, category, invoice_no, link_method, po_number, platform$doc$),
('o2c_grn_lines', $doc$LIVE GRN, normalised -- every row of every partner GRN feed (hot_grn = Blinkit BCPL, hyperpure_grn = Blinkit ZHPL, instamart_grn, milkbasket_grn = Milkbasket, reliance_grn = Reliance Signature and Smart stores AND Metro Cash & Carry (told apart by shipping address; item-level from the GRN PDF lines since 2026-09-23, article via the Milkbasket item map), nb_grn = Nature's Basket, mraws_grn + mrgrn_grn = More Retail, bb_alert_grn + bb_net_grn = BigBasket, flipkart_cb_grn / flipkart_ppr_grn / fatema_grn / slveggies_grn = Flipkart Minutes, matched on PO number across every fulfilment-partner entity, flipkart_quick_grn = the Flipkart Minutes portal PO report (FLIPKART QUICK tab of the Amazon GRN workbook, POs from Jun 2026; platform Flipkart Quick like every Flipkart Minutes entity since 2026-10-19, its FLS... POs are invoiced on C00048 FLIPKART INDIA), matched by PO + FSN, CLOSED / CANCELLED PO lines only, no GRN date, zepto_grn and amazon_grn = portal reports pasted into Google Sheets, matched by PO + item) in one shape, with the PO number cleaned, the invoice reference the partner quoted (invoice_ref_raw), the FY27 invoice it resolved to (invoice_no, match_method; null when the partner quoted a pre-April-2026 invoice, a document number of their own, or nothing), the feed's item code and its ERP item (erp_item_no via ref_platform_item_map; null = unmapped), received_qty (accepted units), ordered_qty, rejected_qty and reject_reason where the feed has them. Use it to audit a single invoice's receipt or to see what a partner quoted. For totals use o2c_bridge, which sums these per invoice x item. No GRN exists for DMart, First Club or trade accounts other than Nature's Basket and the Reliance stores.

Columns: feed, platform, po_number, invoice_ref_raw, invoice_no, match_method, grn_no, grn_date, feed_item_code, erp_item_no, received_qty, ordered_qty, rejected_qty, reject_reason, source_file$doc$),
('ref_customer_invoicing', $doc$LIVE MASTER (business config). One row per ERP customer that has invoiced since April 2026: po_invoice_pattern (ONE_PO_ONE_INVOICE or ONE_PO_MANY_INVOICES -- Reliance / Milkbasket, Nature's Basket, Namdhari's, Metro Cash & Carry, First Club and a few small trade accounts; named by the business or observed as >= 5% of POs with more than one live invoice), grn_feed (which GRN table covers the customer; null = no GRN feed in Supabase) and grn_match_rule (how o2c_bridge ties that feed to invoices), with the observed statistics behind the tag: pos_since_apr26, invoices_since_apr26, inv_per_po, max_invoices_per_po, pct_pos_multi_invoice. platform is the channel_map platform (Trade when none). erp_channel is the ERP's own channel for the customer, bc_customer_card.Customer_Posting_Group: TR-ONLINE (marketplaces and quick-commerce partners), TR-MOD T (modern trade), TR-GEN T (general trade), TR-DIST (distributors), TR-ALTERNATE CHANNEL (corporate / gifting / B2B), TR-OTHER (packaging billing, sampling, wastage). Since 2026-10-19 o2c_sync_customer_ref() keeps the table on every o2c_refresh(): a customer that invoices without a row is added (platform from channel_map, else Trade for every ERP channel but TR-ONLINE; an online customer no rule names keeps platform NULL and grn_match_rule says to add a channel_map_overrides row), erp_channel is refreshed, and rows not marked reviewed follow channel_map when its platform changes. reviewed = true once a person has confirmed the row; re-pushes and the sync never overwrite reviewed rows. Columns: customer_no, customer_name, search_name, platform, erp_channel, po_invoice_pattern, grn_feed, grn_match_rule, pos_since_apr26, invoices_since_apr26, inv_per_po, max_invoices_per_po, pct_pos_multi_invoice, note, reviewed, updated_at$doc$),
('o2c_bridge_live', $doc$ORDER-TO-CASH BRIDGE, LIVE INVOICES ONLY (line grain) -- warehouse.o2c_bridge filtered to invoice_status = 'LIVE'. USE THIS, NOT o2c_bridge, for every order-to-cash question: totals, fill rate, shortage and short-credit lists, "which invoices did PO X produce", any list of invoices or lines. Cancelled invoices are excluded here; they are a re-invoicing artefact (the ERP cancels and re-issues under the same PO with a suffix) and must never be counted, listed or netted anywhere -- neither their quantity nor their value is real. Columns, grain and every meaning are identical to o2c_bridge: read that doc for PO -> INVOICE -> GRN -> CREDIT MEMO, grn_coverage and credit_status. Only go to o2c_bridge itself when the question IS about cancellations or re-invoicing (invoice_status, cancellation_cm_no, replacement_invoice_no, replaces_invoice_no). For invoice-level answers use o2c_invoices_live.

Columns: po_number, po_number_raw, po_suffixed, platform, customer_no, customer_name, customer_search_name, po_invoice_pattern, ship_to_code, ship_to_name, warehouse_code, so_no, invoice_no, invoice_date, invoice_status, cancellation_cm_no, replacement_invoice_no, replaces_invoice_no, erp_item_no, item_name, item_category, po_qty, invoiced_qty, unit_price, invoiced_value, grn_feed, grn_nos, grn_date, grn_qty, grn_rejected_qty, grn_reject_reason, grn_duplicate_rows, grn_match_method, grn_coverage, short_qty, excess_qty, short_value, shgrn_cm_nos, shgrn_cm_qty, shgrn_cm_value, credit_status
platform is resolved at ship-to level (channel_map_locations): Reliance Retail's RRL MILK BASKET locations appear as Milkbasket, its stores and DCs as Reliance. Group by platform and both come out as separate rows.$doc$),
('o2c_invoices_live', $doc$ORDER-TO-CASH BRIDGE, LIVE INVOICES ONLY (invoice grain) -- warehouse.o2c_invoices filtered to invoice_status = 'LIVE', one row per posted sales invoice, FY27. USE THIS, NOT o2c_invoices, for every invoice-level order-to-cash question: how many invoices, invoiced value, GRN status, short_qty / short_value, credit_status, and any list of invoices. Cancelled invoices are excluded and must never be counted, listed or netted anywhere. This is what v_grn_fill_rate and v_grn_pending_invoices are built on, so their numbers and yours agree. Columns and meanings are identical to o2c_invoices -- read that doc. Count invoices with count(*), POs with count(distinct (customer_no, po_number)). Only go to o2c_invoices itself when the question IS about cancellations or re-invoicing.

Columns: po_number, po_number_raw, po_suffixed, platform, customer_no, customer_name, customer_search_name, po_invoice_pattern, ship_to_code, ship_to_name, warehouse_code, so_no, invoice_no, invoice_date, invoice_status, cancellation_cm_no, replacement_invoice_no, replaces_invoice_no, item_lines, po_qty, invoiced_qty, invoiced_value, grn_feed, grn_nos, grn_date, grn_qty, short_qty, excess_qty, short_value, lines_not_in_grn, grn_coverage, shgrn_cm_nos, shgrn_cm_qty, shgrn_cm_value, credit_status
platform is resolved at ship-to level (channel_map_locations): Reliance Retail's RRL MILK BASKET locations appear as Milkbasket, its stores and DCs as Reliance. Group by platform and both come out as separate rows.$doc$);

-- Birbal migrations append to these docs in place; the delete + insert above wipes those appends, so they are
-- re-applied after the insert above (each guarded, so a second run adds nothing).
-- 035 (2026-09-09): INC credit memo = cancelled
update warehouse.warehouse_meta
set doc_md = doc_md
  || E'\n\nCANCELLED means either of two things, and both are excluded from the _live views: BC''s own Cancel/Correct action (invoice header flag, corrective memo, cancellation_kind = ''BC_CANCELLED'', 201 invoices FY27) OR a credit memo posted against the invoice with return reason code INC (cancellation_kind = ''INC_MEMO'', 721 invoices, 485,891 units, Rs 2.17 crore). The second kind carries no BC flag at all -- the accounts team credits the invoice with reason INC instead of using the Correct action -- so it looked LIVE until migration 035. Some were re-issued under the same PO (replacement_invoice_no set) and some were simply credited in full and never re-billed; both are cancelled. cancellation_memo_no names the memo. A cancelled line always carries grn_coverage = ''CANCELLED_INVOICE'', credit_status = ''INVOICE_CANCELLED'' and NULL short_qty / excess_qty / short_value, whichever kind it is.'
where table_name in ('o2c_bridge', 'o2c_invoices', 'o2c_bridge_live', 'o2c_invoices_live')
  and doc_md not like '%CANCELLED means either of two things%';
-- 169 (2026-10-13): cancelled invoice -> re-invoice link, GRN moved to the re-invoice
update warehouse.warehouse_meta
set doc_md = doc_md
  || E'\n\nRE-INVOICES (migration 169): a cancelled invoice and the live invoice raised against the same PO in its place are linked by warehouse.o2c_invoice_replacements. replacement_invoice_no is set on the CANCELLED invoice (the live re-invoice) and replaces_invoice_no on the LIVE re-invoice (every cancelled invoice it replaced); both are NULL elsewhere. A re-invoice carries the cancelled invoice''s po_number when the suffix made them differ (4549479352A -> 4549479352, po_suffixed = true), so it joins its PO line. A GRN the partner booked against the cancelled invoice is MOVED to the re-invoice''s line for the same item (when that line has no GRN of its own): grn_carried_from names the cancelled invoice on the re-invoice''s line, grn_moved_to names the re-invoice on the cancelled line, whose GRN columns are then NULL -- a receipt is on one line only. So a re-invoice is never "GRN pending" or "not in GRN" just because the receipt was booked against the invoice it replaced.'
where table_name in ('o2c_bridge', 'o2c_invoices', 'o2c_bridge_live', 'o2c_invoices_live')
  and doc_md not like '%RE-INVOICES (migration 169)%';
update warehouse.warehouse_meta
set doc_md = doc_md
  || E'\n\neffective_invoice_no (migration 169): the invoice this GRN row counts against in o2c_bridge -- invoice_no, except where the feed matched a CANCELLED invoice that was re-invoiced, in which case the receipt moved to the live re-invoice (see o2c_invoice_replacements).'
where table_name = 'o2c_grn_lines'
  and doc_md not like '%effective_invoice_no (migration 169)%';
-- 183 (2026-10-16): the bridge shows the billed item code; product_item_no is the folded product key
update warehouse.warehouse_meta
set doc_md = doc_md
  || E'\n\nITEM CODES (migration 183): erp_item_no / item_name are the code BILLED on the invoice line. Breads are billed FG/00xx from WH/0007 (Ahmedabad bakes) and TG/00xx ("O ..." names) from every other warehouse; Love Cake FG/0137 and Donut Cake FG/0143 are FG everywhere. product_item_no is the same product folded through item_rename_map (FG and TG of one bread share it): join PO lines, the register, POD sheets or memos on product_item_no, and group by it for any per-product number across warehouses.'
where table_name in ('o2c_bridge', 'o2c_bridge_live')
  and doc_md not like '%ITEM CODES (migration 183)%';
-- Birbal migration 197 (2026-10-21): zero-quantity invoice lines are NOT_SHIPPED, not ITEM_NOT_IN_GRN / SHORT_CREDITED
update warehouse.warehouse_meta
set doc_md = doc_md
  || E'\n\nNOT_SHIPPED (migration 197): an invoice line with quantity 0 -- the PO item rides on the invoice but nothing was shipped -- is grn_coverage NOT_SHIPPED and credit_status NOT_SHIPPED, with NULL short_qty / excess_qty / short_value, unless the GRN lists the item or a short-GRN memo names it. It is neither received, short nor GRN pending: leave it out of any receipt or shortage count. A zero line the GRN does list stays ITEM_QTY.'
where table_name in ('o2c_bridge', 'o2c_bridge_live')
  and doc_md not like '%NOT_SHIPPED (migration 197)%';
update warehouse.warehouse_meta
set doc_md = doc_md
  || E'\n\nNOT_SHIPPED (migration 197): an invoice''s grn_coverage and credit_status ignore its zero-quantity (NOT_SHIPPED) lines, so an invoice whose shipped lines were all received in full is GRN_FULL; an invoice with nothing but zero lines is NOT_SHIPPED.'
where table_name in ('o2c_invoices', 'o2c_invoices_live')
  and doc_md not like '%NOT_SHIPPED (migration 197)%';
